{"resourceIdentifier":"3000","resourceName":"Nankang District MSW Landfill Site LFG Recovery and Comprehensive Utilization Project","description":"Nankang District MSW Landfill Site LFG Recovery and Comprehensive Utilization Project (hereafter referred to as the project) is located in Banling Village, Longhui Town, Nankang District, Ganzhou City, Jiangxi Province, P.R. China. The project is invested, constructed and operated by Ganzhou Baichang New Energy Co., Ltd. The objective is to collect the landfill gas (LFG) from Nankang District MSW landfill site (hereafter referred to as Nankang District landfill site) and utilize it to generate electricity.\r\nNankang District landfill site is located in Banling Village, Longhui Town, Nankang District, Ganzhou City. The project has a total designed capacity 5MW (5*1,000kW) and combusts the LFG, which contains nearly 50% of methane, to generate electricity and export it to the Central China Power Grid (CCPG). The project started construction on 25/04/2021 and started operation on 13/07/2021. The operation period of the project will end on 31/12/2031.\r\nThe project collects and utilizes LFG from Nankang District landfill site for power generation, which would otherwise be released into the atmosphere. Methane in the LFG has been emitted to the atmosphere since the landfill started operation. Therefore the project avoids methane emissions and, at the same time, electricity is generated from a renewable energy source, instead of being provided by the grid. \r\nScenario existing prior to the start of the implementation of the project activity (the same as baseline scenario) \r\n•\tLFG from Nankang District landfill site is released into the atmosphere.\r\n•\tEquivalent electricity generated by the project is supplied by the CCPG, which is dominated by fossil fuel based power plants.","location":{"latitude":25.533373,"longitude":114.811666},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-05-25","